[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Planning a comprehensive data module for the energy systems research post. Mapping six data dimensions:
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] primary energy supply mix, energy trade flows, LNG exports, electricity generation, import dependence, and world primary energy timelines.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Sources will draw from the Energy Institute Statistical Review, IEA World Energy Outlook, and BP/EI datasets.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Drafting narrative
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] angles around domestic sourcing, fuel mixes, and trade flows. Considering headlines like "Fossil fuels still ~80% of primary energy while electricity goes low-carbon faster." Starting to populate the data file with concrete EI 2025 figures, beginning with global primary energy composition.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Global primary energy
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] consumption sits near 620 EJ for 2023 and 2024. Country-level fuel mixes are being mapped: China and India heavy on coal, the US on oil and gas, Japan import-dependent, Norway on hydro and oil exports, Saudi Arabia on oil, and France on nuclear electricity despite oil in primary transport.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Major oil exporters include Saudi Arabia, Russia, the United States, Iraq, Canada, and the UAE.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Top LNG exporters are the United States, Qatar, and Australia. Major importers include China, Japan, India, the European Union, and South Korea. The work will proceed in phases: a rich data module first, then the dashboard, then the post. Dashboard panels will feature a stacked bar chart for primary energy mix by country, a scatter plot linking import dependence to fossil share, grouped bars for net fuel trade flows, and an area chart showing the world primary energy path over time.
[2026-08-20 09:16:57] [cot:thought] Adding a fifth dashboard panel comparing electricity and primary low-carbon energy gaps. An LNG triangle exporters chart will use a donut or ranked layout. Controls will include panel selector, region filter, and fuel toggle. Five chart types are planned: stacked bar, area, scatter, donut, and horizontal ranked bars. Now writing the data module.
